<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary participation.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico has assigned all three direct sales of paper and six repurchase agreements whereby it had sought to drain 3.230 billion pesos from the secondary market on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    364 days   23.12 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    182 days   22.24 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     91 days   21.77 pct</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    400 million     35 days   20.99 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     27 days   20.94 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     25 days   20.99 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     15 days   20.95 pct</p>
<p>    600 million     11 days   21.00 pct</p>
<p>    180 million	1 day    20.36 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
